<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">v0.0.1 · early development · MIT</p>
      <h1>Ruby’s ergonomics.<br>Zig’s runtime.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Fola is a Ruby-like programming language with a bytecode VM written in Zig. You get Ruby syntax and a batteries-included standard library, and a single static binary that also compiles to WebAssembly. Gradual typing is on the way.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="button primary" href="/learn/">Get started</a>
        <a class="button" href="/play/">Try it in your browser</a>
      </div>
      <pre class="install"><code class="language-sh">git clone --recursive <%= site.config["repo"] %> &amp;&amp; cd fola &amp;&amp; zig build</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-code">
      <div class="window">
        <div class="window-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><em>hello.fola</em></div>
<pre><code class="language-ruby">class Greeter
  def initialize(name)
    @name = name
  end

  def greet(times = 1)
    times.times.map { "Hello, " + @name + "!" }
  end
end

Greeter.new("Fola").greet(2).each { |line| puts line }

scores = { ada: 92, grace: 88, linus: 75 }
p scores.keys.select { |name| scores[name] &gt; 80 }
# =&gt; [:ada, :grace]</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features">
  <div class="features-inner">
    <div class="feature">
      <h2>Feels like Ruby</h2>
      <p>Fola parses with Prism, the Ruby core team’s own parser, so blocks, classes, modules and string methods read the way you expect.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h2>Runs on Zig</h2>
      <p>A bytecode VM with inline caches, a tracing GC and arena-allocated ASTs. It compiles to one binary with no system Ruby needed at runtime.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h2>Batteries included</h2>
      <p>JSON, YAML, CSV, files, sockets, HTTP, SQLite, Redis, threads, crypto, i18n and a Rack-style web framework are all built in.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h2>Everywhere WebAssembly goes</h2>
      <p>The same interpreter ships as <code>fola-wasi.wasm</code> and <code>fola-web.wasm</code>. The <a href="/play/">playground</a> runs it in your browser.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-web">
  <div class="home-web-inner">
    <div>
      <h2>A web framework in the box</h2>
      <p><code>Fola::Web</code> includes routing, middleware, ERB-like templates, static files and WebSockets. This website is built with it: a Fola script renders the Markdown, applies the templates and writes every page.</p>
      <p><a href="/stdlib/web/">Read the Fola::Web reference →</a></p>
    </div>
<pre><code class="language-ruby">require 'fola/web'

get "/hello/:name" do |name|
  "Hello, " + name + "!"
end

Fola::Web.call(Fola::Web.app, Fola::Web.env_for("/hello/zig"))
# =&gt; [200, {"content-type"=&gt;"text/html; charset=utf-8", ...}, ["Hello, zig!"]]</code></pre>
  </div>
</section>

